{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they shall send out from the camp.</b> This is the camp of the Shekhinah, for the metzora, the zav, and one defiled by a corpse — who are defiled with a seven-day impurity — are sent out from the camp of the Shekhinah. But in the other camps, which are the camp of Levi and the camp of Israel, the law of the three of them is divided: the metzora is sent out from all three of them, which are the camp of the Shekhinah, the camp of Levi, and the camp of Israel, as we find concerning the metzora (Leviticus 13:46): ״בדד ישב מחוץ למחנה מושבו״ — 'he shall dwell alone, outside the camp shall be his dwelling' — and that is the camp of Israel. The zav and one with a discharge (ba'al keri) are sent out from two of them — from the camp of the Shekhinah and the camp of Levi — but are permitted in the camp of Israel, as the rabbis of blessed memory expounded in Pesaḥim concerning the matter of one with a discharge (Deuteronomy 23:11): ״וכי יהיה בך איש אשר לא יהיה טהור מקרה לילה ויצא אל מחוץ למחנה״ — 'when there is among you a man who is not pure from a nocturnal emission, he shall go out outside the camp' — this is the camp of Levi; all the more so is he forbidden to enter the camp of the Shekhinah. And one defiled by a corpse is sent out from the camp of the Shekhinah alone, and is permitted in that of Levi, and all the more so in that of Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:48.273861227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}